 relate to the situations that the  unrelatable characters find themselves  in season 2 ends with one of those who  hasn't found themselves in a situation  where you're trapped with your family  and it's not easy to get away the roys  can't get away because they're on their  daddy's super yacht and while everyone's  coming together to try to figure out  what to do about the cruise ship  controversy no one here is safe and  everyone involved arrives with different  things on their minds conor and willa  are fresh off opening night of the play  she wrote and he financed which seems  destined for a lackluster reception shiv  is coming off what i guess you would  call a victory for the family where she  convinced the sexual assault victim who  was going to testify not to go through  with it in an effort to spice things up  with her husband she's arranged a  threesome with one of the employees that  works on the yacht roman is coming off  of a hostage situation more or less that  came out of a meeting that he set up in  an effort to get the financing to take  the company private kendall arrives in a  pretty good place he had the strongest  showing at the congressional hearings  and he's got naomi pierce with him as  his companion greg solidifies his place  once again as the outsider by not  realizing that sails out means nails out  and he's got a nail fungus to deal with  on top of his terrible performance at  the hearing that underlines the  situation that logan roy finds himself  in and sets the table for what they all  end up on this boat to do on his way  there logan gets a call where he learns  that the position of some of his big  shareholders is that he should step down  to me it never seems like he considers  this even later when he throws it out as  an option in front of his family but  we'll come back around to that the deal  is the family's still in the middle of  the proxy fight after the takeover that  kendall set in motion before he had to  pull back after 