 assure  him that she wouldn't let anything  happen to him he makes it clear that he  wasn't okay with finding out that shiv  wanted an open relationship on their  wedding night and how he now wonders if  the sad he'd be without her would be  less than the sad he would get from  being with her that marks the end of her  chances to take over as ceo as later she  loses points when she goes to logan to  ask him not to use tom as the sacrifice  things don't go much better for the  other roy's not named logan connor hits  his dad up for a hundred million to help  with things after he refuses to help  with positive reviews for willa's play  he has to endure being crushed in the  process and agree to drop out of the  presidential race logan makes kendall  send naomi away saying he wasn't  properly informed and that he just  doesn't want ken on drugs it's the last  in a long line of awful things he's had  to endure this season starting with  getting pulled out of rehab and then  being forced to go into the house of the  family of the kid that died and it all  sets things up nicely for the end logan  arrives at his decision and tells  kendall even though he did so well at  the hearings he's gonna have to be the  face and that they'll create a press  conference where he can admit that he  knew everything directed the cover-up  and that it went no higher kendall  accepts this and then asked his father  if he ever thought he could do the ceo  job he says that he's not a killer he  stresses you have to be a killer and  then ken throws it out there that maybe  he deserves it for the boy who died and  logan tells him to forget that it's  nothing there was no real person  involved echoing the language that was  used for covering up the cruise ship  crimes ken assures everyone he'll be  okay and then he leaves to go back to  new york with greg he arrives at the  press conference to read the prepared  statement after describing why he's  there he drops a butt the butt hurt  around the world and goes off script  calling logan a malignant presence a  bully and a liar and that he was fully  personally aware of these events for a  number of years he points out that his  father always kept tight control over  everything that happened and that he  would never let settlements of millions  of dollars and payments go out to these  people without knowing about it and  kendall has those documents from greg to  prove it  back on the yacht the family's watching  and you see logan's face it's almost as  if he starts to smile sitting there  seeing his son become a killer he did  the thing that it didn't seem like any  of them would be able to do go against  their dad and really try to bring his  reign to an end kendall had tried to do  it before and we saw how that played out  he spent most of the season as a  punching bag completely cowed and that  kept the others in line everything fell  into place and greg holding on to those  documents finally paid off of course  logan won't go down without a fight his  smile led some viewers to guess that  this might have been his plan all along  i tend to think it's more of a callback  to that season one clip i opened the  video with that he just couldn't help  enjoy seeing his son do what he would  have done if the situation was reversed  i mean i see where people are coming  from and you can kind of make it work if  you go back and look at it that way but  based on how we've seen logan handle  things leading up to this point i think  it would be somewhat out of character he  uses his money his power and his  influence to get what he wants and  everything sort of falls apart when that  doesn't work think of him walking out of  the negotiation with nan pierce when she  tried to force him to name shiv as his  successor which is something that he  told his daughter he'd do at the  beginning of the season and then you  have to wonder if he just would have  told kendall that he thought he could  have been the ceo would he s